 as Gifts or Edges (I would for Gifts to get a better use of the sheet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:26:08-07:00","id":1387454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1387279-superior-character-sheet?p=1387280#post1387280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go for a Standard Talent sheet and treat the powers as Gifts or Edges (I would for Gifts to get a better use of the sheet).</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough, though I may tinker with it. I was a bit confused in regard to Superiors and whether or not they have facets, but I see now that they do. Even without Dramatic Editing (unless they have the Tactician power), they still get all of the other powers that come with Inspiration. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:41:53-07:00","id":1387520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1387279-superior-character-sheet?p=1387454#post1387454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True enough, though I may tinker with it. I was a bit confused in regard to Superiors and whether or not they have facets, but I see now that they do. Even without Dramatic Editing (unless they have the Tactician power), they still get all of the other powers that come with Inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think they have Facets and Inspiration, at least it\u2019s not in the Template not in the Experience table.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s up to me, I would set this as the difference between a Stalwart and a Superior, the first have Inspiration (or a similar Source value), that gives a few advantages, but have to be evolved to grant more advantages, while the second is stronger at first but have less space to evolve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:59:35-07:00","id":1387542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1387279-superior-character-sheet?p=1387520#post1387520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t think they have Facets and Inspiration, at least it\u2019s not in the Template not in the Experience table.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s up to me, I would set this as the difference between a Stalwart and a Superior, the first have Inspiration (or a similar Source value), that gives a few advantages, but have to be evolved to grant more advantages, while the second is stronger at first but have less space to evolve.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its vague in the book. But for them to use Dramatic editing (via the Tactician power), then they need Facets. And if they have Facets, then they have other uses for Inspiration.<br /> <br /> The easiest thing to do would be to limit the Tactician power to two dots, then Inspirations and Facets are a non-issue. Which may be what I will do. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:17:44-07:00","id":1387545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1387279-superior-character-sheet?p=1387542#post1387542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its vague in the book. But for them to use Dramatic editing (via the Tactician power), then they need Facets. And if they have Facets, then they have other uses for Inspiration.<br /> <br /> The easiest thing to do would be to limit the Tactician power to two dots, then Inspirations and Facets are a non-issue. Which may be what I will do.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way Tactictian is worded is pretty clear. Once per session you can use Dramatic Editing. Talents need to spend Inspiration to use Dramatic Editing. Superiors with Tactician don't. They just get to use it once a session without cost. (They also get +2 Enhancement when executing their backup plan represented by the editing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":". 05-11-2020, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:41:25-07:00","id":1387554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1387279-superior-character-sheet?p=1387545#post1387545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The way Tactictian is worded is pretty clear. Once per session you can use Dramatic Editing. Talents need to spend Inspiration to use Dramatic Editing. Superiors with Tactician don't. They just get to use it once a session without cost. (They also get +2 Enhancement when executing their backup plan represented by the editing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. I get it now. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 05-11-2020, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}